{"created": "2026-07-02T04:02:27.012312+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-29T11:35:42.565520+00:00", "id": 21123912, "conceptrecid": "21123911", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21123911", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "metadata": {"title": "When a Basis Goes Stale: Routing Consequence Through Admissibility", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "description": "<p>When a governance basis becomes stale, the question facing any consequence-bearing system is what form of continuation is permissible. Binary suspend-or-proceed models collapse a multi-dimensional decision into a single bit, discarding information that determines whether continuation is ungoverned, admissibility-controlled, or structurally prohibited. This paper specifies a routing matrix for consequence resolution after admissibility failure, grounded in a six-state continuation taxonomy (pass, contain, refuse, suspend, escalate, require re-attestation) with HARD_STOP as a terminal veto, keyed by a base matrix of failure kind against consequence grade, and modified by authority state, reversibility, escalation availability, and policy reference. The specification is drawn from the Aurora-Lens runtime epistemic governance architecture, where the base matrix and modifier pipeline are implemented and tested. Two extension points &mdash; absent ownership as a canonical failure kind, and compound staleness composition rules &mdash; are named as open and given intended design direction without overclaiming implementation status.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Stokes, Margaret", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0004-6422-4174"}], "keywords": ["admissibility, consequence routing, governance architecture, epistemic governance, runtime governance, staleness, delegation, Aurora-Lens, failure taxonomy, consequence grade, re-attestation, AI governance"], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21123911"}}]}}, "title": "When a Basis Goes Stale: Routing Consequence Through Admissibility", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21123912", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21123912", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21123912?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21123912/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21123911", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21123911", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21123911", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21123911", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21123912/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21123912/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912:When_a_Basis_Goes_Stale_Routing_Consequence_Through_Admissibility.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912:When_a_Basis_Goes_Stale_Routing_Consequence_Through_Admissibility.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912:When_a_Basis_Goes_Stale_Routing_Consequence_Through_Admissibility.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912:When_a_Basis_Goes_Stale_Routing_Consequence_Through_Admissibility.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21123912:When_a_Basis_Goes_Stale_Routing_Consequence_Through_Admissibility.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api